Description: CVE-2019-9022 (bug #77369): dns_get_record() took a DNS record with no data (its length 0) and read on with a negative length, a memcpy() past the buffer of the answer; such a record is skipped now. It needs a hostile DNS server or a forged answer
Origin: php-src commit 8d3dfabef459fe7815e8ea2fd68753fd17859d7b (Stanislav Malyshev, 29.12.2018, PHP 7.1.26; in Remi Collet's 7.4 branch), as Debian carries it for 5.6 (php5 5.6.40+dfsg-0+deb8u12 of jessie LTS and its ELTS, debian/patches/CVE-2019-9022.patch)

diff --git a/ext/standard/dns.c b/ext/standard/dns.c
index 027d3f38..2201432e 100644
--- a/ext/standard/dns.c
+++ b/ext/standard/dns.c
@@ -454,6 +454,10 @@ static u_char *php_parserr(u_char *cp, u_char *end, querybuf *answer, int type_t
 	GETLONG(ttl, cp);
 	GETSHORT(dlen, cp);
 	CHECKCP(dlen);
+	if (dlen == 0) {
+		/* No data in the response - nothing to do */
+		return NULL;
+	}
 	if (type_to_fetch != T_ANY && type != type_to_fetch) {
 		cp += dlen;
 		return cp;
